The '''Theed Funeral Temple''' was a small temple on the [[planet]] [[Naboo]] reserved for the [[cremation]]s of the [[Naboo (people)|Naboo]].

==History==
Constructed on the outskirts of [[Theed]], the Funeral Temple was a quiet, reflective place sought out while mourning the [[Death|dead]]. An ancient domed building, the small temple had an open ceiling directly over the pyre at the interior chamber's center. It was at the temple that the [[planet]]'s dead were [[Cremation|cremated]], their lives celebrated by mourners who gathered in a tiered circle around the pyre.<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

In [[32 BBY]],<ref name="SWGA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> following the [[Trade Federation]]'s [[Invasion of Naboo|unsuccessful invasion]] of the planet, [[Jedi Master]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] was [[Funeral of Qui-Gon Jinn|cremated]] in the temple after his death at the hands of the [[Sith apprentice]] [[Maul|Darth Maul]].<ref name="TPM" />

